   "id": "co_arrow_spire",
   "area_id": "co_arrow_peak",
   "name": "Arrow Spire",
   "grade": "5.8",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Counted by one climber among the finest San Juan routes. The crux is pitch one, an amazing 200+ft 5.8 dihedral. Pitch two is easy climbing with a runout, then moves through overhangs. Above, difficulty eases to 5.6 at most. Moving around the towers beneath the summit is exposed and fun. One party rappelled into the notch, got caught in a thunderstorm and retreated via the gully below, which is horrendously loose, downclimbing all but the last 150ft, which they rappelled (the anchors ought to remain). Climbing out of the notch felt like roughly 5.5/6.",
